/**
@namespace CleanTool
@brief CleanTool – AutoCAD cleanup and wall-trim tools.

@namespace CleanTool.Core
@brief Platform-independent rules and algorithms. Has no reference to AutoCAD and is fully unit tested.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Abstractions
@brief Contracts shared by all operations: ICleanOperation, CleanStage, IOperationScope, ICleanLogger.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Geometry
@brief Basic geometry: points, segments, tolerances and affine transforms.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Geometry.Shapes
@brief Comparable shapes (line, circle, arc, polyline, block) that objects are read into.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Hosting
@brief Tool modules and the loader that isolates them from each other.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Model
@brief Object identity and display properties.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Pipeline
@brief Runs operations in stage order, each in its own scope, and reports the results.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Operations.Thickness
@brief Thickness = 0: removes the extrusion of objects (runs before Z = 0).

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Operations.Flatten
@brief Z = 0: moves objects (including floating blocks) to the XY plane.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Operations.Duplicates
@brief Finds and removes exact copies, including copies of block content.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Operations.BlockTrim
@brief WallTrim: cuts loose lines where they run along or through blocks such as columns, and optionally joins
the remaining wall faces into closed outlines.

@namespace CleanTool.Core.Operations.Layers
@brief Deletes unused layers; wildcard matching for name patterns.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool
@brief AutoCAD adapter: plug-in entry point, tool modules, commands, dialogs and gateways.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Hosting
@brief ToolHost: how commands reach the loaded tool modules.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Tools.Clean
@brief The Clean tool: CT_CLEAN, -CT_CLEAN and the quick cleanup commands.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Tools.WallTrim
@brief The WallTrim tool: CT_WALLTRIM and -CT_WALLTRIM.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Composition
@brief Shared wiring: operation factories and registry, runner, settings, the AutoCAD session behind the dialog.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.UI
@brief Shared WinForms dialogs and options pages; independent of AutoCAD types.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Gateways
@brief AutoCAD implementations of the Core ports.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.ShapeReading
@brief Converts AutoCAD entities, their properties and block content into Core shapes.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Flattening
@brief Per-type strategies for moving entities to Z = 0.

@namespace CleanTool.AcadTool.Infrastructure
@brief Session, entity scopes (selection, blocks), transactions, command-line output and logging.
*/
